<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine boosts '97 grain crop forecast to 37 mln T.</title>
<headline>Ukraine boosts '97 grain crop forecast to 37 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine has boosted its 1997 grain harvest forecast to 37 million net tonnes from 35 million, Interfax news agency quoted a senior agriculture official as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>The agency gave no reason for the improved outlook, which it attributed to Deputy Prime Minister in charge of agriculture Mikhailo Zubets.  </p>
<p>Recent heavy rains have hampered the harvest.</p>
<p>Last year's net grain output was a disastrous, drought-hit 25.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
